+/*
+ * RG353VS / MGS2 port notes
+ * -------------------------
+ * Upstream renders into a wl_egl_window-backed EGLSurface, which is the
+ * zero-copy path.  That does not work here: the 32-bit game runs under box86
+ * with libwayland-client in BOX86_EMULATED_LIBS (emulated x86 code), while EGL
+ * is the native ARM Mali driver reached through box86's wrapper.  Handing an
+ * emulated-x86 struct wl_egl_window to the native eglCreateWindowSurface is an
+ * ABI mismatch and wglMakeCurrent faults with 0xc0000005.
+ *
+ * So we render into an offscreen EGL pbuffer and present by copying to a
+ * wl_shm buffer ourselves, with a synchronous glReadPixels straight into the
+ * compositor buffer.
+ *
+ * An asynchronous pixel-pack-buffer path is also implemented here, and it is
+ * OFF by default because measurement on this hardware showed it is a large
+ * regression.  Measured on the same scene, 300-frame samples:
+ *
+ *   MGS2_GL_PBO=0 (synchronous):  23.4-43.6 fps, readback 4.9-6.2 ms/frame
+ *   MGS2_GL_PBO=1 (async PBO):    10.7-12.5 fps, readback 0.09 ms,
+ *                                 but map+memcpy 23.8 ms/frame
+ *
+ * The PBO does exactly what it promises — glReadPixels stops blocking and
+ * drops to 0.09 ms — but Mali hands back the mapped pack buffer as uncached
+ * memory, so reading 1.2 MB out of it costs far more than the 5-6 ms the
+ * direct read cost in the first place.  Keep the code: it is behind one flag,
+ * it is the right shape if a future driver maps cached, and it is how the
+ * numbers above were obtained.  Do not turn it on without re-measuring.
+ *
+ * Note also that presentation was never the dominant cost: at ~23 fps the
+ * frame is ~42 ms and the readback is ~5 ms of it.  The rest is x86 emulation,
+ * game logic and WineD3D.  Further frame-rate work belongs there, not here.
+ *
+ * A rotating pool of wl_shm buffers is likewise available; measurement showed
+ * no benefit over a single buffer (25.0 vs 23.5 fps, inside thermal drift), so
+ * the default is a modest 2 — enough to avoid dropping a frame when the
+ * compositor is still holding one.
+ *
+ * Everything is switchable at runtime through environment variables so the
+ * combination can be A/B tested on the device without a rebuild — device time
+ * is scarce and the console reboots under load.  See mgs_cfg below.
+ */
